  "PublishCopy": {
    "title": "Stop signs used to be yellow (for 30 years)",
    "description": "Picture a stop sign. Red, eight sides, impossible to miss.\nFor 30 years, American stop signs were yellow. The first one went up in Detroit in 1914 as black letters on a white square; the octagon came in 1922; and from 1924 they were yellow because no red paint could survive the sun. Only in 1954 did they turn red, to match the traffic light.",
